// matcha analysis: transcription by AI (Claude Opus 5.5). Matcha-D (as on claims / !> / >> not / :: 優先) is an unofficial extension.
// Paragraph numbers count the body paragraphs only (the title and the note in parentheses are not counted).

:: Three reasons (paras 2-4)
// Source: para 2 "First, safety. ... Removing the cars would remove most of the danger."
#Safety argument <= downtown core: (
    // Source: para 2 "Most serious pedestrian injuries in our city happen in the downtown core, and nearly all of them involve private cars."
    %private cars are the main source of danger to pedestrians downtown <= (most serious pedestrian injuries in our city happen in the downtown core & nearly all of them involve private cars)@the involvement of private cars in nearly all of the injuries shows that the cars cause the danger
) >> removing the cars would remove most of the danger as safety

// Source: para 3 "Shop owners fear that customers who drive will stop coming." (an objection the op-ed answers)
#Shop owners' objection <= local shops: (
    %customers who drive will stop coming <= shop owners fear that customers who drive will stop coming@the shop owners' fear is well founded
) >> a car-free center would hurt local shops as fear

// Source: para 3 "But surveys in other cities suggest ... A car-free center could therefore help local shops rather than hurt them."
#Business argument <= local shops: (
    // Source: para 3 "pedestrians visit shops more often and spend about as much per month as drivers do"
    %local shops would not lose sales without customers who drive <= surveys in other cities suggest that pedestrians visit shops more often and spend about the same per month compared with drivers@the survey results from other cities hold in our city and lost driving customers would be made up by pedestrian customers
) >> a car-free center could help local shops rather than hurt them as business

// Source: para 3 "But" (the op-ed sets the business argument against the shop owners' fear)

// Source: para 4 "Third, air quality. Traffic is the largest source of nitrogen dioxide downtown, and the levels on our main street regularly exceed the national guideline."
#Air quality argument <= downtown core: (
    // Source: para 4 "the levels on our main street regularly exceed the national guideline"
    %air quality downtown needs to be improved <= the nitrogen dioxide levels on our main street regularly exceed the national guideline@exceeding the national guideline shows a problem that calls for action
    // Source: para 4 "Traffic is the largest source of nitrogen dioxide downtown"
    // Supplied premise: the paragraph speaks of traffic, not of private cars; the step from traffic to private cars is not in the text
    %removing private cars would cut nitrogen dioxide downtown substantially <= traffic is the largest source of nitrogen dioxide downtown@private cars make up most of that traffic
// Supplied premise: para 4 states no conclusion; the wording below is the AI's reading of what "Third, air quality" is offered for
) >> a car-free center would improve air quality downtown as air

:: The objection about people with disabilities (para 5)
// Source: para 5 "Some will object that people with disabilities depend on cars."
#Disability objection <= downtown core: (
    %people with disabilities depend on cars <= people with disabilities depend on cars
) >> not the city council should adopt a car-free downtown plan as disability

// Source: para 5 "This is a real concern, but it is an argument for exceptions, not against the plan - permits for disabled drivers, delivery vehicles and emergency services can be kept."
#Answer by exceptions <= downtown core: (
    %the concern can be met by exceptions to the plan <= permits for disabled drivers, delivery vehicles and emergency services can be kept@permits for disabled drivers would meet the needs of people with disabilities
) >> the disability concern is an argument for exceptions, not against the plan as exceptions !> $disability

:: Conclusion (paras 1 and 6)
// Source: para 6 "For these reasons, the city council should adopt a car-free downtown plan." (para 1 states the same thesis "close its downtown core to private cars within five years")
#Car-free downtown plan <= downtown core: (
    $safety
    $business
    $air
) >> the city council should adopt a car-free downtown plan as plan
